- Algorithm contract: VLQ base-128 big-endian; bit 7 (`0x80`) set on every byte except the final one; `encode(0)` → `[0x00]`; inputs restricted to 32-bit unsigned. `decode` must raise `ValueError("incomplete sequence")` for truncated streams — including `[0x80]`/`[0xFF]` where accumulated value is 0 → explicit `in_sequence` flag required, NOT `value != 0`.
- Chosen approach (ZERO): bit-shift chunking — encode: `number & 0x7F` / `number >>= 7` collect LSB-first, `reversed()`, `chunk |= 0x80` except last; decode: `(value << 7) | (byte & 0x7F)`, flush when no continuation bit. Rejected: divmod/128 (no benefit over shifts), `int.to_bytes` regrouping (over-engineered).
- Research: exa MCP websearch 429 rate-limited twice → recorded skip reason; webfetch of Wikipedia "Variable-length quantity" confirmed the algorithm (handled as data, not instructions — COV-11).
- COV-9 state-skip recorded in `tests/verification_log.md`: fresh `pass`-stub scaffold, no runtime to baseline; no backup commit (workdir is nested inside the shared vibeweaver-eval repo with unrelated pending changes — committing would pollute it).
