## What I implemented
`encode(numbers)` → list of ints: each 32-bit unsigned number is split into 7-bit chunks LSB-first, reversed to MSB-first, with `0x80` set on every chunk except the last (`0` → `[0x00]`). `decode(bytes_)` → list of ints: accumulates `(value << 7) | (byte & 0x7F)`, flushes when a byte's high bit is clear, and raises `ValueError("incomplete sequence")` when the stream ends mid-sequence — using an explicit `in_sequence` flag so `[0x80]`/`[0xFF]` (accumulated value 0 but still incomplete) are correctly rejected. Stdlib only, no comments added.

